{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/bad0jytg","slideIndex":8,"position":{"left":75,"top":160,"width":1100,"height":95},"text":"The centroid barrier decreases as C increases and increases with temperature in the cases studied.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#1B2C3A","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/q94zatcv","slideIndex":8,"position":{"left":75,"top":285,"width":1100,"height":100},"text":"The matched finite-P reference is lower than every saved MC barrier. Finite-P bias alone therefore cannot explain the discrepancy.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#1B2C3A","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/lgfip8bi","slideIndex":8,"position":{"left":75,"top":425,"width":1100,"height":105},"text":"Residual well-population imbalance, limited replication and autocorrelation constrain the interpretation. Run-to-run spreads are not confidence intervals.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#1B2C3A","alignment":"left"}}
